ath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129841#post1129841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'd be better off as a vampire then. I'd piss off less people and possibly live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could always.. join the church :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:51:54-07:00","id":1129848,"title":"","content":"Don't be nervous about the Pure to Forsaken ratio on here, guys. Even the books confirm that Pure collectively outnumber the Forsaken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:53:46-07:00","id":1129849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129844#post1129844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> we can come up with a plan later. For now MORE FORUM WOLVES!</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! We need to see more happy puppies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:03:42-07:00","id":1129852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129839#post1129839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Auspice is concerned I would almost certainly be either a Cahalith or an Elodoth. Though most likely the former.<br /> For Tribe, I would probably want to be a Storm Lord, but would probably end up becoming an Bone Shadow instead. As much as I value leadership, if an entirely new world of mystery opened up to me, I'd be most interested in exploring it and interacting with its strange inhabitants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storm Lords are super interesting, especially when they aren't Alpha. It's a mindset that is so fun to play","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:19:52-07:00","id":1129857,"title":"","content":"That one is far harder than the Vampire version, if only because I don't know as much (by far) about the Forsaken as I do about the Kindred (which is sad, considering that if prefer werewolves over vampires in the folklore). Still, there is some things that I'm sure of.<br /> <br /> First thing first, I wouldn't be a Pure. Just their name displease me. I hate peoples who think that they are &quot;better&quot; or &quot;purer&quot; than others for reasons of blood, ancestry, creed or faith. SO, obviously, out with them.<br /> <br /> Now, the Forsaken... it's a little hard, because I don't dig too much the whole &quot;sin of the father&quot; angle they have. In the same time, they have things to back up their stories, even their hated enemies believes that they have indeed sinned in the past... so I could either be a Forsaken or a Ghost Wolf leaning toward them. So, I guess it would be something like that.<br /> <br /> Auspice : Cahalith<br /> <br /> I like to tell stories. I love to learn about history, legends and all. Obviously, Luna would see it fitting to make me pursue my passion in her service (or she could be fickle and says &quot;Hey, you've got some times when you let your anger get the best of you ! Why don't you become a Rahu ?)). But she wouldn't be like that, right ? Right ?<br /> I'm not much of a fighter, nor a fit addict, but I'm not too out of shape for my age, so I pretty much thinks I would be an adventurous Cahalith. I would probably write down the history of my pack and our discoveries in the form of fantasy novels so as to prevent humans from learning about us by accident.<br /> <br /> Tribe : Bone Shadows<br /> <br /> I'm a lore nut, and so are they. A perfect match ! Plus, I tend to believe in the &quot;mundane&quot; supernatural (gypsy cruses, amulets, spirits, etc.), so I think I could join them pretty easily, even while maintaining my belief that the world must be made better socially and environnementaly. <br /> <br /> Usual life : As a Werewolf, I would probably help my pack to claim and then protect our territory... if I can get some privacy at times. I really need some moments of solitude to read and contemplate and think and create. I would also seek to forge beneficial pacts with minor spirits, learning the First Tongue and trying to convince humans to better the place my pack and I would call our territory. For my tribe, I would try to discover ancient knowledge, first locals and then globals.<br /> <br /> As an elder Werewolf : I would be trying my best to pass down informations and knowledge to the younger Uratha, while lamenting their lack of care for such history earned at the risk of our pelts by my packmates and I.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:27:13-07:00","id":1129867,"title":"","content":"I usually choose Ithaeur for these. Since second edition others have become a lot more appealing, my character is an Elodoth. But I think for myself I'd still go Ithaeur. It would be a significant change to my life but it would probably be the most 'me.' Cahalith would be a close second.<br /> <br /> From there, I think I'd probably go Bone Shadow. I like some of the concepts behind the Pure, and they're certainly a lot more palatable than they were in first edition, but I'm still not a fan of the society, and while as a werewolf I'd certainly get into the killing mode, I'd never be a 'kill all humans,' person. Knowing about Pangaea (do I know? do I keep my knowledge of the books?) would probably be a big impact on my outlook as a werewolf, too.<br /> <br /> I would still end up going Bale Hound. Definitely through a lodge this time, though I might be up for another option if there's a Bale Hound tribe. So far, lodges seem the most appropriate way to handle them. They appeal to me the way the Fire-Touched used to, as a zealous belief system. <br /> <br /> My neighborhood probably wouldn't last long in terms of territory, it would have to be expanded, but I guess alone it would be tougher to spread out if there was neighbors. Still, I'd want to range further for sacred hunts, there hasn't been many murders here throughout history and vicious animal attacks would gain attention. The spirits in my area would have to be tamed as well. I have no idea what it would be like as an elder werewolf. I always had a dream for my werewolf character where they sought out every Maeljin to seek enlightenment in all of the sins, sort of become a 'shining example' of each aspect a Maeljin represents, in the end becoming a type of dark champion for them among werewolves. Basically a villainous inversion of Ultima IV. That would probably be a bit much for me, but it would be an interesting path to power and seems fitting for werewolf second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:37:52-07:00","id":1129868,"title":"","content":"Short and sweet: Iron Master Irakka, since as I said in the vampire thread I'm a sneaky sunovagun, and what concerns me most tends to be human evils, so that would likely be my preferred prey for a hunt.<br /> <br /> I'd sooner be a Ghost Wolf than Pure. Come at me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:56:23-07:00","id":1129878,"title":"","content":"Lots of Bone Shadows... though that one who would be a Bale Hound.. I was wondering when we would see one of them XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:04:45-07:00","id":1129883,"title":"","content":"I think the Blood Talons are too 'about killing' for most people to want to go after. And the Hunters in Darkness are a better fit for Chronicles than the real world, we don't really have sacred places we want to protect as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:12:24-07:00","id":1129888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129883#post1129883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Blood Talons are too 'about killing' for most people to want to go after. And the Hunters in Darkness are a better fit for Chronicles than the real world, we don't really have sacred places we want to protect as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Talons are super interesting, they have a culture of violence and war that appeals so much to base human nature though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:19:10-07:00","id":1129894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129868#post1129868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd sooner be a Ghost Wolf than Pure. Come at me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, I posted a forsaken version of myself first. Both the forsaken and pure me reflects aspects of myself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:53:50-07:00","id":1129909,"title":"","content":"Skimming the 2ed Core, I find myself, surprisingly, drawn to the Elodoth, purely by the fluff of it. Irraka or Rahu work, too, but Elodoth definitly fits me the well, probably the most (close second would be Irraka).<br /> So let's got with Elodoth.<br /> Of the tribes, the Bone Shadows seem like something I might end up in, as the spirit of Exploration and Knowledge-gathering it entails speaks to me, albeit I might join the Hunters in Darkness purely to be part of the Lodge of the Hook Hand.<br /> However, let us for now assume a Bone Shadow Elodoth as I am now, and an Hook Hand Hunter in Darkness Irraka if I could chose.<br /> <br /> So, what kind of Uratha would I be?<br /> Unsurprisingly, I would be the guy trying to learn stuff about this new world, learn how to deal with spirits and how to keep them in check; I'd try to charter new waters, and try to keep peace and unity both within my pack, and with other packs.<br /> Does not mean I would stop thinking about how I could take you down should you become a threat, or that I have a problem with taking the other side in a confrontation, even if that side is not exactly my own beliefs - I quite often take a contrary position in discussion simply because I enjoy debating, something that drives some people nuts =) My secondary role would be to mingle, get information. I usually establish connections to other people quite quickly, and if you throw me into a room of a people, chances are I will come out with having made a few friendly acquaintances - even if it was a meeting of e.g. football (for the americans: soccer) enthusiasts (something I have zero interest in). I can muster some interest for anything, if necessary, at the very least for the passion people have for something. Those connections aren't very deep though - I'd probably be the connection burner type, despite lacking the necessary charisma you'd need for that imo.<br /> I've always been a fan of fighting, and fighting styles, especially barehanded and old-school weapons like sword, staffs and axes, and practised, tried out and dabbled in some myself. Seeing how that would become more important in my new lifestyle, I would definitly do a lot more fighting and physical training.<br /> I do not know if I'd keep my current path in life - I feel I would definitly want to stay/go back to University, and enroll in something like History or Computer Science, to acquire some additional skills that could come in handy. Alternatively, I might go back to the Military, to brush up other skills like Survival, Firearms and Expression.<br /> <br /> Don't know enough about elders yet, but I assume I would be the guy that others would come to ask for help in settling a dispute, or a fair judgement. I'd also consider it my responsibility to take cubs in and give them some much needed assistance, by directing them to the right mindset, helping them ask the right questions. Afte all, giving answers is never as good a lesson as figuring it out for yourself.I wouldn't necessarily infringe on the Spirit laws and stuff, since many of that is Ithaeur territory, but there are many things cubs need to learn. A diplomat, and a teacher, basically.<br /> <br /> As Irraka, this would only chance insofar that eliminating foes would rise up in priority, so I would focus more on becoming stealthy and deadly. Doesn't mean I cannot help people talk it out, but my means would be different. Also, as an Irraka Elder, I would be a dangerous Assassine, but I'd still try and make sure young cubs know how to step and not make tons of noise, how to strike so that there won't be a reply, and relay my experiences in general.<br /> <br /> At least, that is my current impression, haven't finished the book (not by a long shot) yet, so... take this with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Elodoth seems pretty accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:58:02-07:00","id":1129914,"title":"","content":"Giving this a try (keep in mind there are many things i don't know about forsaken so there could be some misinterpretation on my part)<br /> <br /> The most important thing that will go toward my werewolf identity would be my auspice. Which would be much more important to me than my tribe or even my pack.<br /> <br /> So first the auspice:<br /> I'm big into wisdom as a virtue but i think that for my auspice i would be an Irraka. In general I prefer not being noticed and I actually need to make a specific effort to make noise when i move so that i dont startle people. Also (and that could just be in my head) i have the feeling that i can tell where peoples blind spots are and i feel more comfortable there. The more i think about it the more that i feel irraka is the choice for me.<br /> <br /> Next the pack:<br /> Although i, myself, likes cunning and wisdom, i actually think i'd prefer to be in a pack that values honor and wisdom. <br /> <br /> Last the tribe:<br /> No tribe really sticks out to me sadly. I could come back to the fact i value wisdom highly and join the bone shadows and i'm certainly into the investigative aspect of the hunt, so that could work. But i'm not really interested in hunting spirits above others (i find the host more interesting). Also i have this thing where i really dont like showing weakness in front of others (which i think is a storm lord thing?). <br /> I have to say, unless there is some social pressure from packmates or other werewolf into joining a tribe, i likely either wont bother at all or try to learn about all the tribe and be a marginal member of each. (is it like vampire where you can have status into more than one covenant, well tribes in this intance???).<br /> <br /> Last last, the lodge:<br /> I don't know which lodges there are but if there is one about learning secrets, forbidden knowledges (or really any knowledges, the forbidden ones are just generally more fun) and history then i'd join that lodge.<br /> <br /> So in the end, the most important thing for me is the auspice. To be chosen and given a role that suits me and that i'm expected to follow would go a long way toward making me feel ... calmer about myself, with a better sense of purpose i guess. Ugh, i'm having trouble expressing this well sorry. <br /> Anyway the short of it is that my auspice would do more toward defining who i am than my tribe would. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:56:19-07:00","id":1129936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129914#post1129914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last last, the lodge:<br /> I don't know which lodges there are but if there is one about learning secrets, forbidden knowledges (or really any knowledges, the forbidden ones are just generally more fun) and history then i'd join that lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably a few. One that fits would be the Lodge of Scrolls, who hunt 'humans who arm themselves not with weaponry but with knowledge and influence, especially those who possess eldritch lore.' They likely take the knowledge as part of the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:52:19-07:00","id":1129964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129936#post1129936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's probably a few. One that fits would be the Lodge of Scrolls, who hunt 'humans who arm themselves not with weaponry but with knowledge and influence, especially those who possess eldritch lore.' They likely take the knowledge as part of the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lodge of Doors fit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:22:50-07:00","id":1129975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129867#post1129867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would still end up going Bale Hound.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aww, I forgot about Bale Hounds. Now I'm not so sure if I wouldn't have gone with them over the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> Going back to tweak my submission a bit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:43:49-07:00","id":1129990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129867#post1129867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually choose Ithaeur for these. Since second edition others have become a lot more appealing, my character is an Elodoth. But I think for myself I'd still go Ithaeur. It would be a significant change to my life but it would probably be the most 'me.' Cahalith would be a close second.<br /> <br /> From there, I think I'd probably go Bone Shadow. I like some of the concepts behind the Pure, and they're certainly a lot more palatable than they were in first edition, but I'm still not a fan of the society, and while as a werewolf I'd certainly get into the killing mode, I'd never be a 'kill all humans,' person. Knowing about Pangaea (do I know? do I keep my knowledge of the books?) would probably be a big impact on my outlook as a werewolf, too.<br /> <br /> I would still end up going Bale Hound. Definitely through a lodge this time, though I might be up for another option if there's a Bale Hound tribe. So far, lodges seem the most appropriate way to handle them. They appeal to me the way the Fire-Touched used to, as a zealous belief system. <br /> <br /> My neighborhood probably wouldn't last long in terms of territory, it would have to be expanded, but I guess alone it would be tougher to spread out if there was neighbors. Still, I'd want to range further for sacred hunts, there hasn't been many murders here throughout history and vicious animal attacks would gain attention. The spirits in my area would have to be tamed as well. I have no idea what it would be like as an elder werewolf. I always had a dream for my werewolf character where they sought out every Maeljin to seek enlightenment in all of the sins, sort of become a 'shining example' of each aspect a Maeljin represents, in the end becoming a type of dark champion for them among werewolves. Basically a villainous inversion of Ultima IV. That would probably be a bit much for me, but it would be an interesting path to power and seems fitting for werewolf second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sort of Archaon the Everchosen for the Bale Hounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:14:51-07:00","id":1130007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129990#post1129990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sort of Archaon the Everchosen for the Bale Hounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, to a point. He's not about ending the world, neither are the Maeljin. And my tentative agreement is just based on the first section of <a href=\"http://warhammerfantasy.wikia.com/wiki/Archaon\" target=\"_blank\">this entry</a>, as I don't know anything about them from anywhere else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1129975#post1129975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, I forgot about Bale Hounds. Now I'm not so sure if I wouldn't have gone with them over the Predator Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have been my choice when I was younger, but I much prefer the comforts of modern society now. Totally different group between them and Bale Hounds, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Overlooking your post, you would probably want the Blood Talons. Bale Hounds and even Predator Kings aren't about combat, that's pretty much solely the domain of the Blood Talons. And one can be a Forsaken without feeling guilty about what ancestors did. Luna doesn't exist to make you feel guilty, she's there to try and teach you how to survive, through the Oath of the Moon, which ideally keeps you from the extreme ends of Harmony and, thus, losing yourself.<br /> <br /> Also the Sundering happened about 6000-7000 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-16-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:31:28-07:00","id":1130011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130007#post1130007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, to a point. He's not about ending the world, neither are the Maeljin. And my tentative agreement is just based on the first section of <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://warhammerfantasy.wikia.com/wiki/Archaon&quot;]this</a> entry[/URL], as I don't know anything about them from anywhere else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They would have been my choice when I was younger, but I much prefer the comforts of modern society now. Totally different group between them and Bale Hounds, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Overlooking your post, you would probably want the Blood Talons. Bale Hounds and even Predator Kings aren't about combat, that's pretty much solely the domain of the Blood Talons. And one can be a Forsaken without feeling guilty about what ancestors did. Luna doesn't exist to make you feel guilty, she's there to try and teach you how to survive, through the Oath of the Moon, which ideally keeps you from the extreme ends of Harmony and, thus, losing yourself.<br /> <br /> Also the Sundering happened about 6000-7000 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made the comparison to this Bale Hound due to his being the champion of Chaos Undivided rather than being the bringer of the end times. After all the nine Maeljin are pretty much the Chaos Gods in Werewolf 2nd Ed, not counting Dihar level Idigam ( still sad that we will never get to see how powerful Gurdilag was <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), and being equally favored by all nine is pretty damn astounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:43:24-07:00","id":1130016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130011#post1130011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made the comparison to this Bale Hound due to his being the champion of Chaos Undivided rather than being the bringer of the end times. After all the nine Maeljin are pretty much the Chaos Gods in Werewolf 2nd Ed, not counting Dihar level Idigam ( still sad that we will never get to see how powerful Gurdilag was <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), and being equally favored by all nine is pretty damn astounding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah in that regard, totally, especially with the impossible trials for each.<br /> <br /> We do know Gurdilag was Rank 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T15:53:23-07:00","id":1130019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130016#post1130016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah in that regard, totally, especially with the impossible trials for each.<br /> <br /> We do know Gurdilag was Rank 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be Herculean to say the very least. It's funny though, if you think about it, all of the others sort of inadvertently empower Thurifuge, which is funny to me.<br /> <br /> Yeah, but that tells us precisely... nothing. We know his Rank, Bane, and that he was morbidly curious about Souls... but that's it. I want a Dark ages supplement that deals with Gurdilag, considering that he controlled Denver for THIRTY years before Max Roman and Rachel Snow destroyed him. We could see him fully stated out. <br /> <br /> Anyway, back to more Uratha lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-16-2017, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T16:35:11-07:00","id":1130037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130007#post1130007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Overlooking your post, you would probably want the Blood Talons. Bale Hounds and even Predator Kings aren't about combat, that's pretty much solely the domain of the Blood Talons. And one can be a Forsaken without feeling guilty about what ancestors did. Luna doesn't exist to make you feel guilty, she's there to try and teach you how to survive, through the Oath of the Moon, which ideally keeps you from the extreme ends of Harmony and, thus, losing yourself.<br /> <br /> Also the Sundering happened about 6000-7000 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> According to the Werewolf lore, sure. But in real life, Pangaea broke apart 200 million years ago, give or take. I don't see any difference between the Werewolf's interpretation of history to that of Adam and Eve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I was going to describe myself as a Blood Talon originally. And if I had joined the Forsaken, you're right, I'd be a Blood Talon shaman. But then I gave it some more thought and realized that I'm more in line with the Pure than the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The most important thing to me in this universe is my personal freedom. I refuse to acknowledge anybody, mortal or otherwise, who would pass judgement upon me for living my life the way I choose to. My idea of paradise is a universe without consequences; where I'm basically free to do literally anything I please, (something to look forward when we get to <b>Me as a Mage</b>). Plus, I already mentioned outright that I have a low opinion of humanity to begin with, so Harmony means less to me than it otherwise should. I might try to maintain a level of sentience so that I don't go on a suicidal rampage, but that would be the extent of my concern on the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't misunderstand me, though, I'm in no way saying I would be an unrepentant sociopath. I do have a personal code of honor that I try to abide by. For example, I don't care about losing a fight, as long as my opponent won through honorable means. And I generally give people the same degree of personal freedom that I expect of myself. So long as they are not directly inconveniencing me, they're free to do whatever they want. I only get involved when the problem begins to affect my comforts.<br /> <br /> As a Predator King, my problem with the Forsaken would be pretty standard to the book. I don't care that they're associated with some ancient traitors who honestly could have just offered to HELP, rather than murder Father Wolf. My problem would be their insistence on preserving a world that stifles my capacity to be the werewolf I want to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T18:48:18-07:00","id":1130075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130037#post1130037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Werewolf lore, sure. But in real life, Pangaea broke apart 200 million years ago, give or take. I don't see any difference between the Werewolf's interpretation of history to that of Adam and Eve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pangaea is not the Pangaean continental mass, it's another world, between the spirit and the real one. It was detailed in the Neolithic Age of the Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The most important thing to me in this universe is my personal freedom. I refuse to acknowledge anybody, mortal or otherwise, who would pass judgement upon me for living my life the way I choose to. My idea of paradise is a universe without consequences; where I'm basically free to do literally anything I please, (something to look forward when we get to <b>Me as a Mage</b>). Plus, I already mentioned outright that I have a low opinion of humanity to begin with, so Harmony means less to me than it otherwise should. I might try to maintain a level of sentience so that I don't go on a suicidal rampage, but that would be the extent of my concern on the matter. </div> </div> </div>Rampages happen at the high and low ends of Harmony, but yes the Pure do flux between.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't misunderstand me, though, I'm in no way saying I would be an unrepentant sociopath. I do have a personal code of honor that I try to abide by. For example, I don't care about losing a fight, as long as my opponent won through honorable means. And I generally give people the same degree of personal freedom that I expect of myself. So long as they are not directly inconveniencing me, they're free to do whatever they want. I only get involved when the problem begins to affect my comforts. </div> </div> </div>My point with the Blood Talons over the Predator Kings was that the Blood Talons are about fighting. The Predator Kings are about the hunt. The Talons will train you and teach you to fight and have some great warriors, while the Predator Kings have great warriors mostly due to attrition. They don't teach fighting so much as force you to fight to survive, with those who can't find a way out of it falling to the wayside, or more likely never being recruited at all.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings really sound more your style based on your survivalist-intent. Bale Hounds are another thing entirely. Once you step into lodges, you step into cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-16-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:32:30-07:00","id":1130088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130075#post1130075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pangaea is not the Pangaean continental mass, it's another world, between the spirit and the real one. It was detailed in the Neolithic Age of the Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rampages happen at the high and low ends of Harmony, but yes the Pure do flux between.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My point with the Blood Talons over the Predator Kings was that the Blood Talons are about fighting. The Predator Kings are about the hunt. The Talons will train you and teach you to fight and have some great warriors, while the Predator Kings have great warriors mostly due to attrition. They don't teach fighting so much as force you to fight to survive, with those who can't find a way out of it falling to the wayside, or more likely never being recruited at all.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings really sound more your style based on your survivalist-intent. Bale Hounds are another thing entirely. Once you step into lodges, you step into cults.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, I didn't know about that.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I don't have any of the fluff material stuff for Chronicles. I just bought the core books, and the only splat that's up to date is Beast. So there is a craaaaap load of material that I'm not informed about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, I do enjoy fighting, but I don't have any professional education in how to do so. The closest I ever came was white belt Tae Kwon Do, and that was way back in elementary school. And the only thing I remember from that is high block / low block. My personal approach to fighting is based on raw instinct. My style isn't even a legitimate style, it's completely improvised. If I'm in a particularly foul mood, I just shut out the world and let blind rage take the wheel. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't. But that sounds like what the PK's tend to utilize as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:48:34-07:00","id":1130095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130088#post1130088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I do enjoy fighting, but I don't have any professional education in how to do so. The closest I ever came was white belt Tae Kwon Do, and that was way back in elementary school. And the only thing I remember from that is high block / low block. My personal approach to fighting is based on raw instinct. My style isn't even a legitimate style, it's completely improvised. If I'm in a particularly foul mood, I just shut out the world and let blind rage take the wheel. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't. But that sounds like what the PK's tend to utilize as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it's probably rather telling that you bring up Tae Kwon Do and my instinctual response is to crack a big grin and have my inner martial artist go &quot;Fellow Student!&quot; Tae Kwon Do is my foundational and primary style, and my instructor is very practicality focused. I've picked up a little Kung Fu, Kajukenbo, Jeet Kun Do, and Escrima in the twelve years since I've started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:55:10-07:00","id":1130100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130095#post1130095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, it's probably rather telling that you bring up Tae Kwon Do and my instinctual response is to crack a big grin and have my inner martial artist go &quot;Fellow Student!&quot; Tae Kwon Do is my foundational and primary style, and my instructor is very practicality focused. I've picked up a little Kung Fu, Kajukenbo, Jeet Kun Do, and Escrima in the twelve years since I've started.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Congratulations! I sometimes wonder what might have happened if my parents had the money to continue paying for the lessons. Back then, the dojo had all the belts on display on a rack, and I think there was some kind of 'silver' belt that went above black belt. Still don't know what that was about.<br /> <br /> Although I'm a bit confused on the nature of Jeet Kun Do. I used to think it was a fighting style, but now I'm hearing that it's actually a philosophy. <i>&quot;keep what is useful, discard what is useless&quot;</i> or something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:16:12-07:00","id":1130106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130100#post1130100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations! I sometimes wonder what might have happened if my parents had the money to continue paying for the lessons. Back then, the dojo had all the belts on display on a rack, and I think there was some kind of 'silver' belt that went above black belt. Still don't know what that was about.<br /> <br /> Although I'm a bit confused on the nature of Jeet Kun Do. I used to think it was a fighting style, but now I'm hearing that it's actually a philosophy. <i>&quot;keep what is useful, discard what is useless&quot;</i> or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;silver&quot; belt is probably just a school thing. Each instructor has their own philosophy about gradings and how to test for them. And that's a fairly accurate way of looking at Jeet Kun Do. Bruce Lee has been described to me by his student's student as a veritable martial arts prodigy who could be... impatient with anyone less quick to pick things up than he was; he also had very little patience for what he saw as extraneous tradition and sought to do away with it, a big no-no in the conservative martial arts world, but it's an attitude that's become more adopted over time. The instructor I worked with said that his\u200bown master had more than a few stories about what a cocky punk Bruce Lee could be, and how he liked to go out of his way to pick fights by hitting hard, fast, and first. Maybe the philosophy comes across better in print than when it is given by someone with what was by all accounts a pretty abrasive attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:37:03-07:00","id":1130113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130088#post1130088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I didn't know about that.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I don't have any of the fluff material stuff for Chronicles. I just bought the core books, and the only splat that's up to date is Beast. So there is a craaaaap load of material that I'm not informed about. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, you said so in your first post about what you would be. I'm not trying to be harsh in correcting you, though I'm sure I come off that way sometimes. I'm just fixing some misconceptions. I'd hardly expect you to read the entire book, and the Pack, just for this thread. Though I do assert that Forsaken is a great game and quite enjoyable to play. Given your interests you might really enjoy it yourself. But in the meantime I was just clearing muddied things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:42:27-07:00","id":1130117,"title":"","content":"Auspice I couldn't tell.<br /> I submit myself to the ever-wise and ever-mad moon for that judgment. I can easily see aspects of all five auspices in myself, so none of them would be a bad fit, and I'd accept our celestial patron's decision. I'm withdrawn enough as a person to fit as an Irraka, but have enough anger-issues to be a Rahu. I'm creative enough that Cahalith would fit, but I'm also superstitious and spiritual enough that Ithaeur wouldn't be bad either. And Elodoth, standing there in the middle, being a little of everything, and on the balance would therefore also fit.<br /> <br /> Tribe is easier, but not easy. I am quite certain I'd join either the Iron Masters or the Bone Shadows. Both have a core of curiosity and intellectualism that attracts me. I believe in ghosts, and I'm quite certain I've seen them a few times, and I am very curious about this part of the universe, so that is a pull of the Bone Shadows... But on the other hand, I'm more than a little bit a coward, and leaving humanity behind is a scary thought, so I might be drawn to the Iron Masters, just for the familiarity of mankind.<br /> <br /> In the end, I'm quite certain I'd end up as a hybrid case, fitting both tribes. Likely joining one tribe, and a lodge tightly knit to the other. Such as Bone Shadows and Lodge of Scrolls, or Iron Master and Lodge of Death.<br /> <br /> I know I'd learn the nature gifts early, for the Pack Kin and Beast Ride facets. I like animals, and I would enjoy getting closer with them, my pet cats in particular - provided they survive my First Change of course. When I find the limits of that, a search for Predator gifts, properly communicate with them will likely be a goal for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T21:59:18-07:00","id":1130138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130117#post1130117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like animals, and I would enjoy getting closer with them, my pet cats in particular - provided they survive my First Change of course. When I find the limits of that, a search for Predator gifts, properly communicate with them will likely be a goal for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast Talker Wolf Gift. Nice one for that. Skinthief would let you permanently take the form of a cat, instead of a wolf, but that does require a dead cat (though it doesn't have to be yours), so that's a bit morbid, no one wants their pets hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:50:06-07:00","id":1130151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130113#post1130113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, you said so in your first post about what you would be. I'm not trying to be harsh in correcting you, though I'm sure I come off that way sometimes. I'm just fixing some misconceptions. I'd hardly expect you to read the entire book, and the Pack, just for this thread. Though I do assert that Forsaken is a great game and quite enjoyable to play. Given your interests you might really enjoy it yourself. But in the meantime I was just clearing muddied things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, you didn't seem harsh. Though I know using plain text is hard to properly convey emotions during topics like these. It was helpful to get a more accurate description of situation.<br /> <br /> One of the major reasons I didn't get into the game is because I had just come straight from vampire, which I was already moderately familiar with. I had absolutely no idea what to expect jumping into Werewolf. It seemed a lot more complicated at the time, with having a lot more stuff to keep track of than I did in the previous game. In retrospect, I don't think it was that dramatic of a shift from what I remember. They probably just changed the names of stuff around and my brain misinterpreted it at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:45:12-07:00","id":1130187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130138#post1130138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast Talker Wolf Gift. Nice one for that. Skinthief would let you permanently take the form of a cat, instead of a wolf, but that does require a dead cat (though it doesn't have to be yours), so that's a bit morbid, no one wants their pets hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Forgot about that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T06:22:34-07:00","id":1130225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130106#post1130106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's a fairly accurate way of looking at Jeet Kun Do. Bruce Lee has been described to me by his student's student as a veritable martial arts prodigy who could be... impatient with anyone less quick to pick things up than he was; he also had very little patience for what he saw as extraneous tradition and sought to do away with it, a big no-no in the conservative martial arts world, but it's an attitude that's become more adopted over time. The instructor I worked with said that his\u200bown master had more than a few stories about what a cocky punk Bruce Lee could be, and how he liked to go out of his way to pick fights by hitting hard, fast, and first. Maybe the philosophy comes across better in print than when it is given by someone with what was by all accounts a pretty abrasive attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now that I know you do Martial Arts, you are even more likeable to me, Arcanist =D<br /> Many people don't know about the... less likeable aspects of Bruce Lee. In the end, he was human, he did good things (spreading Chinese Martial Arts to the Western World) and bad things (often arrogant, basically betrayed ancient tradition for his own gain etc.). I ain't denying his fame, but don't overgloryfy what was a remarkable, but not flawless human being. (Also kinda sick of people over-estimating his ability. Bruce was amazing, but not unbeatable.)<br /> I like to think of Jeet Kune Do as something similar to MMA, but without the focus on a competitive sport and instead a focus on Self-Defense.<br /> <br /> Blood Talon Irraka sounds fun, too, now that I think about it....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:50:30-07:00","id":1130258,"title":"","content":"While this is late, as I looked over the Fire-Touched Gifts I realized just how terrifying I would be at High Primal Urge. Being a dark prophet of the Shadow bringing the joyful word of Taga Dan is great.. but being able to split the heavens and the earth asunder with some simple spirit magic as well as inspiring madness and/or courage and peace among friend and foe alike like a plague... as well as inciting unyielding rage effortlessly... I'd be a lunatic force of giggling nature.. and if I was pissed enough, I'd be happy to turn into a localized fluffy apocalypse for a few minutes if it led to a few dead Forsaken here or there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:34:41-07:00","id":1130372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130258#post1130258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is late, as I looked over the Fire-Touched Gifts I realized just how terrifying I would be at High Primal Urge. Being a dark prophet of the Shadow bringing the joyful word of Taga Dan is great.. but being able to split the heavens and the earth asunder with some simple spirit magic as well as inspiring madness and/or courage and peace among friend and foe alike like a plague... as well as inciting unyielding rage effortlessly... I'd be a lunatic force of giggling nature.. and if I was pissed enough, I'd be happy to turn into a localized fluffy apocalypse for a few minutes if it led to a few dead Forsaken here or there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Villains have the best parties. Heroes are just jealous they didn't get invited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:00:49-07:00","id":1130385,"title":"","content":"Is it weird that is easier for me to imagine a radical shift in my mindset caused by being roused to a spiritual metamorphosis into a ruthless hunting and killing machine via arguably arbitrary cosmic forces than being selected by an immortal blood drinker to be initiated into the Night Society?<br /> <br /> Fear is a major motif in my life, and understanding it and its power is something I've dedicated a large portion of my life to even if I am not someone who wields intimidation tactics in my interpersonal or professional relationships. I am at heart a storyteller and a student of fear, with a technology skill set and native understanding of human propensity for making the world worse off.<br /> <br /> Imagine a world where some actions had metaphysical consequences in the same way dumping toxic sludge and scum into water reservoirs in the material world would. That's the world Chronicles of Darkness takes place in, from the Hisil savvy point of view. It has an entire invisible ecology being subject to human disruption and contamination, and we know how well humans take care of ecosystems they are aware of, imagine the affect they'd have on one they could easily affect but didn't even knew existed.<br /> <br /> All of that adds up to being most inclined to be a Cahalith, and choosing/fitting best with the Iron Master Tribe.<br /> <br /> A Iron Master Cahalith that shares a lot in common in his hunts as serial killers do with theirs is how I 'd imagine the First Change would affect me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-17-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:03:08-07:00","id":1130388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130372#post1130372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Villains have the best parties. Heroes are just jealous they didn't get invited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's the morality of being a hero","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:19:33-07:00","id":1130397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130385#post1130385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird that is easier for me to imagine a radical shift in my mindset caused by being roused to a spiritual metamorphosis into a ruthless hunting and killing machine via arguably arbitrary cosmic forces than being selected by an immortal blood drinker to be initiated into the Night Society?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not at all. One's a spiritual awakening of sorts, and the other is being inducted into a secret society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:33:57-07:00","id":1130406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130385#post1130385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird that is easier for me to imagine a radical shift in my mindset caused by being roused to a spiritual metamorphosis into a ruthless hunting and killing machine via arguably arbitrary cosmic forces than being selected by an immortal blood drinker to be initiated into the Night Society?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think its weird but it's an interesting difference in the games.<br /> <br /> Like Nyrufa, I think the way it comes about is pretty big. Even the weird 'spontaneous embraces' seem less like 'you've come into your own' and more like 'you lost something important to you, and that place where it was is now filled with hunger.' Even if, in both cases, you're driven by a supernatural compulsion that will most likely end in bloodshed.<br /> <br /> It's like the Werewolf book says, 'Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.' The downsides are usually more of a result of things you do in the game, rather than what you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:13:04-07:00","id":1130429,"title":"","content":"Upon reading more, I thought adding my chosen Blood and Bone would be a good addition.<br /> I believe I would have either Soldier or Destroyer for Blood, and either Hedonist or Gurur for Bone.<br /> Going by my gut instinctis, it would be Destroyer and Guru.<br /> So a Destroyer/Guru Bone Shadow Elodoth. Sounds nice enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw: cannot wait for the <b>You as a Mage</b> thread.<br /> Especially the Archmage part O__O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T05:04:15-07:00","id":1130778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130429#post1130429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon reading more, I thought adding my chosen Blood and Bone would be a good addition.<br /> I believe I would have either Soldier or Destroyer for Blood, and either Hedonist or Gurur for Bone.<br /> Going by my gut instinctis, it would be Destroyer and Guru.<br /> So a Destroyer/Guru Bone Shadow Elodoth. Sounds nice enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw: cannot wait for the <b>You as a Mage</b> thread.<br /> Especially the Archmage part O__O</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be happening today, though truth be told, I'm not as big a Mage fan as some peeps, so that'll be a challenge lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:39:11-07:00","id":1131030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1130778#post1130778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might be happening today, though truth be told, I'm not as big a Mage fan as some peeps, so that'll be a challenge lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here. Other than Beast, Vampire and Werewolf, I have only rudimentary knowledge about the other game lines that I've picked up from wiki sites.<br /> <br /> Though given the context of the setting, I suppose we don't have to worry about Sin Eater, Promethean, Mummy or Demon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've got Mage the Awakening 2nd edition on my Wish List, though I'm really hoping Changeling comes out, first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-18-2017, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T15:18:28-07:00","id":1131904,"title":"","content":"Soooo... What I am hearing is &quot;We will open it later&quot;, yes? :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:32:45-07:00","id":1132004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1131904#post1131904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo... What I am hearing is &quot;We will open it later&quot;, yes? :-D</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's what the others would prefer. <br /> <br /> I was toying with the idea of creating a You as a Beast thread. If anybody feels ready to move onto that one?<br /> <br /> <br /> Been getting a bit of insight into the nature of my dreams over the last year or so. Perfect timing for the subject to come up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:34:31-07:00","id":1132118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1132004#post1132004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If that's what the others would prefer. <br /> <br /> I was toying with the idea of creating a You as a Beast thread. If anybody feels ready to move onto that one?<br /> <br /> <br /> Been getting a bit of insight into the nature of my dreams over the last year or so. Perfect timing for the subject to come up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To quote ancient wisdom: Why not both? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T03:13:59-07:00","id":1132145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1132118#post1132118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To quote ancient wisdom: Why not both? :-)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I got the Beast thread started up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1132144-you-as-a-beast\">You as a Beast</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T06:15:37-07:00","id":1132176,"title":"","content":"Let's see... I can losee my mind since I'm not really stable and harmonious person, or become Bale-hound for evilulz or just Ghost Wolf no one cares aboutique which. In better scenarious - Cahalith (for looney creppy strange guys that's ok) Iron Master (I like city more than village).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:11:01-07:00","id":1133575,"title":"","content":"I certainly feel like I'd end up going straight Rahu Blood Talon. I remember still how good it felt in high school and after basic, just to have that muscle mass it gave me. The endurance I earned. I'd want that back, as a wolf, and I'd have the ability to push myself to limits that even back then I was scared of. Honor is important to me, so Blood Talons makes sense, and the physical emphasis I'd push myself into, the demand for challenge- I can see it. Why rahu? I am a warrior. I'll always be a soldier first, no matter what I do.<br /> <br /> There is a risk that I could fall to the Predator Kings. I love tech, but the pure power of the Dire Wolf would be very tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:18:05-07:00","id":1134854,"title":"","content":"If I where to become a Werewolf myself I believe I would have been born Elodoth because of my political and diplomatic nature, while it has been my downfall but also my focus in life as well. The Iron Masters would track me down after my violent change into the monster and try and help me to enter the world of Urban Survival but as I grow older I will see the broken state of the Forsaken and while my sympathy does lie with them I still see cloying morons fighting over territory and killing spirits who could be put to use. I may begin to stalk Pure wolves trying to understand their view point but find them to be even worse than the Uratha of the Forsaken Tribes. So as I grow older I will begin to see things like the Kindred and Magi populations but begin to understand they are even more ignorant of the big picture than my kin, I will continue to stay in the Iron Masters as a journalist/politician for the Tribe and hope to create a more unified front against the Pure even making deals with creatures such as the Kindred and Magi who I can find some sympathy with, newly embraced kindred especially I find much sympathy for due to my feeling of knowing what that feeling of losing your humanity is like. The greater goal I have in mind is to bridge the gap between the Forsaken and try to help them put aside differences to create a larger more connected nation of werewolves (very similar to the Garou Nation from Apocalypse). My personal life as a werewolf would be incredibly hard with my problems of impulsiveness that I would have to temper with my auspice but I think there would easily be times I refuse to let me rage stay back, all in all I think if I became Uratha I would have an incredibly hard time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T06:35:49-07:00","id":1135748,"title":"","content":"I'd probably be a ghost wolf who lives on the outskirts of everything and is seldom heard from. Probably goes insane after a decade or so and is put down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:04:11-07:00","id":1135769,"title":"","content":"I hate everyone and I worship death.<br /> Predator King.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:46:11-07:00","id":1135789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1135769#post1135769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate everyone and I worship death.<br /> Predator King.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Bale Hound of Wrath","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:59:46-07:00","id":1135797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1135789#post1135789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Bale Hound of Wrath</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, I'm really focused on turning my negative feelings in primal force for my boxing and mma training and my excursions. <br /> I also live in a modern tribe, rejecting a lot of human stuff and concepts.<br /> But I don't really want to talk here about it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T11:14:11-07:00","id":1135846,"title":"","content":"Helur's got it.<br /> <br /> Wrath ain't about hate, it's about anger. Granted the two can be related but Dire Wolf, patron of the Predator Kings, has always had hate in him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T21:27:16-07:00","id":1136489,"title":"","content":"Thurifuge, patron of Violence would take in someone like that in a heartbeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:19:47-07:00","id":1136648,"title":"","content":"I would presumably be a very, very dead human on account of having written all this stuff for a roleplaying game about Uratha society that turned out to be alarmingly accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:22:24-07:00","id":1136650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1136648#post1136648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would presumably be a very, very dead human on account of having written all this stuff for a roleplaying game about Uratha society that turned out to be alarmingly accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooh, thats a nice concept tho. A ghost wolf somehow part of network zero that tries to share the truth by making a roleplaying game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T21:06:04-07:00","id":1137912,"title":"","content":"If I were a werewolf at this point in my life, I'd have to go with the Storm Lords as a tribe because the past five years have been nothing but forcing myself into bettering my life/situation/skills and enduring some of the hardest experiences of my life without letting them break me down. In terms of Auspice, it's tough. I originally wanted to say Ithaeur, or even Cahalith - but ultimately: it's the Rahu. I fight, and I challenge when someone tells me 'you can't do that because of X reason' -- it's how I went from being a D-student in high school, to leading seminars in Honors Program in College. I didn't accept the lot life was giving me, and I changed it. Wish I'd changed it sooner but, hey, maturity isn't a standard thing!<br /> <br /> Storm Lord Rahu Nurse-Woof, yeeeeeeeah.<br /> <br /> edit: I have been informed by a dear friend that Iron Masters would be a better fit, but what do they know? Pfft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 09-06-2017, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T19:31:39-07:00","id":1138477,"title":"","content":"I am incredibly glad that this thread has allowed people to explore this question in such a creative manner, its super interesting and entertaining!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T19:09:09-07:00","id":1139072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1138477#post1138477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am incredibly glad that this thread has allowed people to explore this question in such a creative manner, its super interesting and entertaining!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, and I'm glad we were all at least partially comfortable to showcase some of the less positive aspects about ourselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:44:39-07:00","id":1140400,"title":"","content":"Ooo, I've been hoping one of these &quot;Imagine yourself as this splat&quot; threads existed for Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I actually did a little research on this, because you don't get to choose when you undergo the First Change. So I decided to look up the phase and position of the moon on my birthday, and also have a tribe picked out based on what Renown I favor most. So I choose Bone Shadows because Wisdom is the Renown I personally value the most. And interestingly, I discover that I was born under a waning Crescent, so I'm an Ithauer. <br /> <br /> Except I'm not. The moon actually set a little after noon on the day I was born, and didn't rise until about 2 in the morning on the day after I was born. So by my own self-imposed logic, I'm not a Bone Shadow Ithauer... I'm Pure. Specifically a Fire-Touched.<br /> <br /> My siblings and I are the products of two storied Fire-Touched dynasties coming together. As the eldest, a lot of attention was always riding on me to be an Uratha. It was my destiny to undergo the First Change, and bring glory to the Anshega and my ancestors. In time, I do undergo the Change... but only a few years later, my sister does as well. Both of us tend towards the spiritual: learning the ways of the spirits, befriending them. My brothers never Change, they will make fine mates for some lucky ladies one day. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which... well, my family will never take the fact that I have almost no interest in women well, so I leave. I don't become any less certain that Luna is a crazy bitch who led the Forsaken astray... but I'm more willing to talk first, skin them alive after. They aren't evil, just terribly misguided sinners who have to repent- either by letting us remove the Moon Bitch's taint, or by dying. Up to them. But at the end of the day, we are all children of Father Wolf, so I'm down for the occasional truce or team-up; just more opportunities to convince them that the Pure are where it's at.<br /> <br /> As an elder, I'm probably one of those strangely helpful Fire-Blooded. Always willing to give a word of advice to the pups. But I'm probably running some sort of cult that looks like one of those little one-church denominations. Which I'm the pastor of, naturally. While the normies think I'm preaching about the need to get right with God, I'm really speaking to the occasional Ghost Wolf or Forsaken who stumbles in to the church by accident or a whim. <br /> <br /> And no Forsaken is going to screw with me, because buddy? I've got friends in the spirit courts you wouldn't believe. Make a move, moon-cur, and I'm going to unleash the local insanity and murder spirits on your beautiful family and make you watch as they tear each other apart. Do. Not. Fuck. With. Me.<br /> <br /> Hm. So apparently my background translated into an Uratha context means I wind up as the stereotypical corrupt/gay pastor. Who knew?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:05:59-07:00","id":1140406,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> Luna would still see the first change. It'd take a rite to preclude your auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T16:39:18-07:00","id":1141251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1140406#post1140406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6498_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6498\" data-vbnamecard=\"6498\">Haberdasher</a> Luna would still see the first change. It'd take a rite to preclude your auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well seeing as I already said I would probably be Fire-Touched, branding auspice marks to remove them is a Fire-Touched thing, right? I could see myself being one of those Fire-Touched who get a little too carried away with the branding, going shirtless at tribe functions to show them off: &quot;Yeah it's painful, but if you muscle past the pain, there's actually this awesome endorphin high- wait, why are you looking at me like that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T23:34:49-07:00","id":1141329,"title":"","content":"Yeah! Scorched earth, mother fuckers!<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc06.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2010/294/b/7/werewolf_fire_by_rock0n-d318r8v.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Oh, that's right, I'm Predator King... <i>possibly Bale Hound</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attac