Oh hey honey! I'm just taking Tabitha and Yellow-Eyes out for their morning run! * has a pair of wolf cubs on leashes *&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm rather amused that you deigned to not even humor my joke xD</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re the alpha of this pack so I am used to your idle threats XD. And my family must be pretty bizarre since you have my male sides wife and my children with them, my female sides husband and my children with them, my wereblooded mates for each side of me and my pups with them. All living in that big family compound/mansion together. It would certainly make for interesting sibling dynamics amoung my children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-02-2017, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T13:30:33-07:00","id":1146150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1146020#post1146020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You\u2019re the alpha of this pack so I am used to your idle threats XD. And my family must be pretty bizarre since you have my male sides wife and my children with them, my female sides husband and my children with them, my wereblooded mates for each side of me and my pups with them. All living in that big family compound/mansion together. It would certainly make for interesting sibling dynamics amoung my children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'd have to exert authority then- can't be lenient all the time.<br /> <br /> This also brings up a question I overlooked in the first post, family. I'm pretty sure that I would not try to have biological children, due to the ever present threat of the Forsaken either killing or kidnapping my cubs. However, as I am a dedicated Fire-Touched I would be more than happy to do as the tribe always has done; &quot;adopt&quot;. I would be more than happy to rescue the younger wolf-blooded children of the enemy and raise them as my own. Having youngsters of my own irl has taught me a great deal of patience, and I have no doubt that I would be a loving surrogate father until these rescues were old enough to be claimed by our tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T15:23:25-07:00","id":1149246,"title":"","content":"thinking about it my auspice (if i have one) I could be Elodeth or Ithaeur, more likely Ithaeur i reckon.<br /> As to Tribe i have little idea although i like the idea of either Bone shadows or Iron masters, but tbh i could be a ghost wolf, i think being one of the pure is unlikely, I don't get religion (it's not my thing) so Fire touched are out, Ivory Claws are right out, no way, bit fascist for my tastes and that's putting it lightly - say no to Eugenics - and well the predator kings are a bit to brutal for me, i mean i'm a vegetarian, i don't think their diet would work for me.<br /> <br /> I dont know enough about lodges if I'm honest, none of the ones in the 2nd ed core book or the pack appealed to me, but as others have said a lodge devoted to hunting knowledge is very me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T16:46:15-07:00","id":1149267,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12845_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12845\" data-vbnamecard=\"12845\">ahather</a> being a werewolf in general doesn't agree with being a vegetarian if you want to have even the slightest bit of power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T01:09:47-07:00","id":1149342,"title":"","content":"in which case I'm probably some sort of changing breed, either bear based or based on some sort of herbivore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T19:55:57-07:00","id":1149591,"title":"","content":"Well, always an option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T04:03:11-07:00","id":1149642,"title":"","content":"I mean i also said ghost wolf, and a sincere wish not to chow down on any animals is probably a good reason as any not to join a tribe, most/all of them would seem to expect that sort of diet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T21:17:30-07:00","id":1151205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1149642#post1149642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean i also said ghost wolf, and a sincere wish not to chow down on any animals is probably a good reason as any not to join a tribe, most/all of them would seem to expect that sort of diet</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not a tribe thing, it's a werewolf thing. When you become one, you're suddenly part fleshy-creature and part spirit and that spirit-half doesn't really give a rat's behind about your distaste for meat, or that you weren't really keen on this hunting business and you'd really like it if every three months you didn't feel the need to chase down some hapless prey-thing.<br /> <br /> At best, you can stay at Primal Urge 1 and have no restrictions on your feeding habits and be as vegetarian as you'd like to be... but if werewolf-you is that morally concerned about eating meat, you're probably also going to be dealing with some strange Harmony issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 10-20-2017, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:39:44-07:00","id":1151227,"title":"","content":"Yes. Mechanically the prohibition comes from your Primal Urge, the 'power stat' for werewolves. At 1 you're fine, but 2-3 you can only eat meat, at 4-5 raw meat, 6-7 the meat of carnivores, 8-10 Essence, which you get from the sacred hunt or going humanitarian.<br /> <br /> To be fair to you, I believe the change would not only come in the form of a sudden restriction, but also a sudden urge to eat these things.<br /> <br /> But if you really wanted to keep your eating lifestyle, you might be able to find a spirit who could help out, but it would involve a very close and long-lasting bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T00:25:50-07:00","id":1151232,"title":"","content":"one of the changing breeds would probably better for OC me then, as much as i love this game i would not get on well with being uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:37:31-07:00","id":1151337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1151232#post1151232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the changing breeds would probably better for OC me then, as much as i love this game i would not get on well with being uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or you could go with being a Beast-kith Changeling. If it's the wolf you resonate with, you could have that without the predatory drive that comes with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:09:12-07:00","id":1151347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1151337#post1151337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or you could go with being a Beast-kith Changeling. If it's the wolf you resonate with, you could have that without the predatory drive that comes with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Until Frailties kick in at least","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T13:03:08-07:00","id":1151434,"title":"","content":"I mean there is too much of an abuse metaphor with CtL, for we to be comfortable imagining my self as one (playing a character is another matter). Tbh I resonate far more with bears, for they are also large and fluffy, and omnivorous (apart from polar bears and pandas)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T13:03:30-07:00","id":1152267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1151434#post1151434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean there is too much of an abuse metaphor with CtL, for we to be comfortable imagining my self as one (playing a character is another matter). Tbh I resonate far more with bears, for they are also large and fluffy, and omnivorous (apart from polar bears and pandas)</div> </div> </div> </div>Werebears are pretty varied","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T13:45:30-07:00","id":1152287,"title":"","content":"that was my though, i like bears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T09:00:45-07:00","id":1152524,"title":"","content":"As much as I hate Changing Breeds, the Storm Bears were easily one of the most terrifying things aside from the hummingbird people. They would be an awesome alternative to a Blood Talon Werewolf lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T10:48:06-07:00","id":1152556,"title":"","content":"need 2nd ed changing breeds that isn't broken, and has functional fluff.<br /> a storm bear is probably what i would be paradoxically as a werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:37:14-08:00","id":1157640,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Alright, I have given myself some time to think about this, so lets see what I think Werewolf-Me would be like. This is going to be a long one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>tl;dr</b>: I would probably be an Elodoth of the Storm Lords or Iron Masters. I would likely be a pack alpha or second, taking on leadership responsibility as it becomes necessary. Assuming I keep my current knowledge before my First Change, I would be obsessed with the <i>Idigam</i> - I would have immense respect and fear for their power, and I would believe that they are a force that must be hunted and destroyed. While my pack and I handle immediate threats, I will save a portion of my resources, contacts, and favours so that when the time comes to hunt an <i>Idigam</i>, I will not go in blind and empty-handed. My hope would be to form a new tribe that is better equipped to hunt them (at the very least with an appropriate gift and Siskur-Dah rite-master bonus). While there may be other Firstborn totems to find, Creator Wolf represents an excellent totem on a thematic level - wielding the power of order and creation against a force of chaos and destruction. She also makes an easy first choice of a potential totem given that there are already stories about her and Destroyer Wolf. I would also have a less hostile stance towards the Pure for two reasons. The first is that I would rather direct them towards fighting <i>Idigam</i>. The second is that I am unlikely to believe much of the oral history of werewolves, and as such I am likely to see the Pure/Forsaken conflict as a conflict over stupidity. That said, I would not join the Pure unless I were Cahalith (which I would take as Luna telling me that she doesn\u2019t want me to join the Forsaken). Of course, I would not trust the Pure - I mean lets be honest, they wouldn't inherently trust me any more than any other Forsaken werewolf, and would kill me just as readily.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Auspice</b>: Of all supernatural creatures of the Chronicles of Darkness, the werewolf is the only one I feel confident about picking their supernatural \u2018birth\u2019 trait for myself (for example, I would not be comfortable picking a vampire clan because while I would like to be Mekhet in that instance, I don\u2019t get to chose who embraces me). The Auspice still isn\u2019t really something that I get to pick for myself, but it is usually based on the werewolf\u2019s personality so I actually feel like I could answer this with a reasonable chance of being correct.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think that I would be an <b>Elodoth</b>. I am pretty good at mediating conflicts, and I am usually very good at seeing every side of a conflict. Also, unlike quite a few of the people who have thus far answered, I lack a belief in the spiritual and supernatural. I am a university student who studies biophysics - I am quite scientifically driven and tend to have a more materialistic mindset that suits the resources and abilities of an Elodoth. When I say materialistic mindset, I mean that I focus on the material world, and I focus on that which can be understood through the scientific method of conducting experiments and seeing how nature responds to my prods. I also find the metaphor of the web of connections to be quite apt: &quot;He never misses an opportunity to study and master the web of connections that binds everything in his territory, because he never knows which string in that web he might have to pull \u2014 or break. This, unfortunately, has the disadvantage of making the Elodoth feel personally unconnected to everyone and everything, with the possible exception of his pack.\u201d I also identify with the Elodoth mindset of considering every set of laws and deciding which is best for the situation - whether it be the Oath of the Moon, human law, spirit law, a mix of the above, or whatever else might be appropriate. It\u2019s all a matter of perspective in that regard.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That said, I would be okay with any auspice except for Cahalith. As an Ithaeur, I could imagine myself as a sort of spirit scientist, and I would treat the Shadow as a newly discovered aspect of the natural world. I would also be very interested in studying the nature of essence - is it a physical thing with properties that can be measured? Can such an instrument be crafted with human technology if one only knows where to look? If I were an Ithaeur, I would be interested in finding out. That said, most Ithaeur are highly spiritual before their first change, and I simply do not fit that bill. I would be okay with Rahu - I would prefer to act as a strategist and fight with ranged weapons. The problem is that most Rahu are confrontational before the first change, and I prefer to avoid confrontation or to be a mediator to other people\u2019s confrontation. I would be okay with Irraka as a very close second, as I am quiet and difficult to notice. I would also consider myself to be asocial (although not antisocial). That said, I don\u2019t really have the Irraka mindset of always looking for and prodding for weakness - maybe I would develop it if I were to become an Irraka werewolf.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I don\u2019t think I suit Cahalith very well. While I like telling stories and creating well enough, I am too quiet to be Cahalith. I think I could manage the lore keeper aspect of being a Cahalith, but that is only half their role. The inspiration and glory aspect of being Cahalith doesn\u2019t suit me. Being the heart and soul of a pack doesn\u2019t suit me. I know the Cahalith who is jealous of the Rahu is the typical stereotype, but I would be jealous of every other auspice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tribe</b>: I see myself most likely as a member of the Storm Lords or the Iron Masters, although it also depends on the tribal allegiance of other werewolves in my area, and if I can pass their rites of initiation. I find it quite possible that I may just stay as a Ghost Wolf while doing my best to maintain good relations with the Forsaken (and the Pure if at all possible, but then again I doubt it). Assuming I get to keep my knowledge of the World of Darkness when I become a werewolf, the realization that the <i>Idigam</i> exist would be terrifying to me, and I would want cultivate as many allies as possible for the coming storm.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Regarding <b>Storm Lords</b>, I am the sort of person to take on responsibilities that I believe need to be claimed. Last year I involved myself in my school\u2019s politics, and I did it because no one else would take on the role. I don\u2019t think I would be the sort of stereotypical Storm Lord macho alpha. I would rather be second to a competent leader than to be the leader. That said, I think being a Storm Lord is in part about taking the responsibility of leadership when it is necessary, that they need to be strong for their friends and their pack. The whole point of \u201cAllow no one to witness or tend to your weakness\u201d is about being strong when it is easier to be weak - when your pack sees that you are strong, they will be strong too. I think I can inspire in that sense - leading through action, through taking responsibility and empty positions of leadership that no one else will take.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Others have mentioned that they don\u2019t care for the whole \u201csins of the father are levied onto the son\u201d garbage that Luna and the Forsaken dump on each other. I don\u2019t care for it either. I probably wouldn\u2019t even believe in the whole Pangaea myth. I mean the reason that I should care about keeping the balance between Flesh and Shadow is because a bunch of wolf spirits killed a wolf god some time around 5000BCE? Who cares? That's 7000 years ago! Get over it! The fact that spirits seem to agree with this story would have given me pause in the past, but Dark Eras makes it pretty clear that the oral history of the werewolves is pretty flawed, and spirits are hostile enough to werewolves (certainly Forsaken) that I shouldn't take them at their word under most circumstances. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Instead, I would feel it to be my responsibility to maintain the balance that the Forsaken strive to maintain in order to aid and protect humanity from the Shadow, leading to Iron Masters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Regarding <b>Iron Masters</b>, I think I would make a good fit there because of my more scientific and materialistic mindset, as well as my fondness for humanity. Humans in general run the gambit from awful, stupid, and lazy to wonderful, clever, and ambitious, and as a former human I would feel that the powers and abilities I gained should be used to help humanity (which would in turn help myself - for as humanity advances, the Iron Masters adapt with them). I would probably still consider myself to be human, even though werewolves are not considered to be humans. I don\u2019t imagine it would take me too long to get used to hunting humans and human institutions that obstruct humanity either in Flesh or Shadow. Sometimes humanity has to be protected from itself, after all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think it quite possible that I would first join the Iron Masters, and then later join the Storm Lords as an Evocatus. The Tribes of the Moon book present that Storm Lords take in veterans of other tribes, and in fact recreate the prospective werewolf\u2019s initiation rite as a sign of respect to the werewolf\u2019s original tribe (although they also make these recreations much more challenging than before). I\u2019ve also read that Red Wolf doesn\u2019t doesn\u2019t take it too hard when a werewolf leaves the Iron Masters. If I were to take this route, I would essentially act as a member of both tribes, taking advantage of the skills I learned as an Iron Master and doing my best to maintain good relations with them. Later I will bring up the Lodge of Scrolls. I would like to maintain good relations with this lodge - even if I do not join them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I could see myself working closely with both of these tribes, but I would do my best to maintain contacts with the other Forsaken Tribes. Each Forsaken Tribe has its use in the hunt. Bone Shadows have a lot of spirit lore, and if I could have access to even a fraction of it I would be quite happy. I would want to learn how to fight other werewolves from the Blood Talons if I could - Empty Wolves are quite scary. There is also a lodge in the Hunters of Darkness called the Lodge of Harmony whose goal of keeping the <i>Idigam </i>locked away coincide with my goal of destroying them or otherwise removing them as a threat. As such, I would be interested in maintaining contacts with the Hunters in Darkness - particularly the Lodge of Harmony.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think there is a possibility I would remain as a <b>Ghost Wolf</b>. I would be interested in finding a new Firstborn totem to help me hunt the <i>Idigam</i>. The Creator Wolf fascinated me when I first heard of her, but if she is Rabid Wolf (or otherwise already taken) then I suppose I\u2019d just have to find another Firstborn or something of relatively equal power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If Luna deigned to curse me with the Cahalith auspice, I would take it that she wants me to join the Pure Tribes and that she doesn\u2019t want me to be Forsaken. In such a case, the only option for me is <b>Ivory Claws</b>. I am not enough of a fanatic to join the Fire-Touched, and loosing access to the craft of humans is enough that Predator Kings gets an instant pass. To be fair, I don\u2019t think I fit the Ivory Claws all that well aside from my access to resources.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That said, I have read Korogra's Homebrew Pure Tribe - the <b>Fang-Shapers</b>. Even over the official 3 Pure Tribes, this is the one that I would be most likely to join ( I mean this as a complement; I like your homebrew tribe). I feel like Creator Wolf would have made an excellent opponent to the <i>Idigam</i> thematically, I do think that the servants of the God-Machine was a clever choice for the tribe\u2019s sacred prey, so good on you there. I also think you have it right that Creator Wolf would not be bound to a Forsaken Tribe. It was after the death of Urfarah that Destroyer Wolf and Creator Wolf were separated and Creator Wolf was tormented by spirits of madness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Lodges</b>: I like the <b>Lodge of Scrolls</b>, although I would definitely have to get used to writing down everything I see and hear in order to make an effective scroll-keeper. If I didn\u2019t join this lodge, I would still hold respect for it and do my best to support their agenda, especially since I probably wouldn\u2019t put too much stock in the oral history of the Uratha. I say it\u2019s about time that werewolves start writing their history and knowledge down and keeping track of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I also like the <b>Lodge of Salvation</b> to a certain degree. Practically speaking, I think the Pure are more useful as meat-shields against the <i>Idigam</i> than as enemies of the Forsaken. Aside from that, my lack of belief or concern for most of werewolf mythology and oral history would lead me to believe that there is really no good reason for the Forsaken and Pure to be at each other\u2019s throats. I don\u2019t know that I would make an effective member of this lodge, but I would support their actions, and I would try to find a rite that would restore the Pure's auspice, or allow them to convert their Pure renown into Forsaken renown (bad enough that they can't keep their renown). The problem is that I think that efforts I make to convert a member of the Pure would only make things worse. That said, it would be harder for Pure captives - or Pure werewolves in general - to insult me and get under my skin.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If I knew enough about the <b>Lodge of Harmony</b>, I would be a staunch supporter of their efforts to cage the <i>Idigam</i> that they are aware of.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think the <b>Lodge of Crows</b> would appeal to me if I were ever able to find out that it exists. I wouldn\u2019t know if I were being considered as a prospect, but cunning is one of the types of renown that I would favour, and glory is the one renown that I would be happy enough to avoid, so who knows? Of the Three Pillars of the Storm, I think this the one I am most suited to. That said, it is not for me to judge my suitability to join this lodge. I'll just have to do my thing and see what happens.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Blood and Bone</b>: With regards to Blood, of the available default choices I think it would most likely be <b>Fox</b>. I\u2019m not necessarily comfortable with the idea that I would abandon my pack, but I think it\u2019s fair enough to say that I would rather be cautious and clever than brutal and in-your-face. Perhaps I would be a hybrid of Fox and The Monster? It\u2019s less about running from a fight than it is taking a more advantageous position. Let the Rahu be the Destroyer - I say. I\u2019ll use my connections and resources. I\u2019ll use cleverness and cunning to flank the foe and cut it off from its resources and allies. I\u2019ll be the tactician rather than the brute, and if I have to fight I will fight dirty. I will harass, target weak spots, fight unfairly, and I will use my gifts and my ability to push werewolves in and out of death rage to what I think would be the best effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As for Bone, I think that of the available choices, I would most likely be a <b>Wallflower</b>. It would give me great satisfaction to bring plans into motion from the shadows, to have a solution to problems before my pack brings the problem up. I don\u2019t very much enjoy the spotlight, but I will take it if it is necessary to do so. I would take the position of pack alpha if I felt no one else was competent enough to do so, but I\u2019d rather be the second. I suppose in that sense, <b>Guru</b> would make sense as well, given its focus on practical advice as opposed to spiritual advice. Perhaps a mix of the two, but it\u2019s hard to know for certain what my Blood and Bone would be - after all, who knows what confidence I would gain with the brute strength of a werewolf, but these are my best guesses based on what I am like now.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Young Wolf</b>: This depends on how much of my previous Chronicles of Darkness and Werewolf the Forsaken knowledge I retain after my First Change. Ultimately it would be necessary for me to join a pack. My goal within the pack would be to rise in the hierarchy either to alpha or second. I would of course manage the Elodoth responsibilities of the pack, but there are aspects of the werewolf condition that fascinate me enough that I would help the Ithaeur with rites and rituals. With regards to renown, I would focus on Honor, Cunning, and Wisdom, and I would leave Glory for the Rahu and Cahalith.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">While rites are the domain of the pack Ithaeur, I may still hold some interest in learning rites and developing at least one of my own. For example, silver serves as a powerful bane against werewolves, and forms terrible wounds that burn and that heal slowly. 1e had the Rite of Healing for the purposes of healing aggravated wounds, but 2e does not. I would be interested in coming up with such a rite, or improving upon an already existing version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If I make it through the First Change with my knowledge of the <i>Idigam</i> in tact, I would be obsessed with them. My spiritual touchstone would be the <b>Hunt against the <i>Idigam</i></b>. I would consider the <i>Idigam</i> to be my own personal sacred prey, and even though they are essentially gods that I could never hope to defeat by myself, I would still focus on learning their weaknesses, finding ways to distinguish them from other prey, spinning a web of contacts and allies that could potentially be of help, and doing whatever else I could to arm myself against these beings. This is where my Wallflower Bone would come into play. While the pack focuses on immediate affairs (and I would of course contribute to dealing with these affairs), I would always keep the <i>Idigam</i> in mind. Here and there I would save some resources for the <i>Idigam </i>fund. I\u2019ll save favours for fighting the <i>Idigam</i>, calling in allies to help me fight and contacts to arm me with knowledge. If I don\u2019t know about <i>Idigam </i>beforehand, I\u2019ll start preparing once I learn about them and once I come to respect and fear their power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I would fight the Pure if they got in my way, but I would prefer not to. As I said before, mainly due to my opinions on the oral history of the werewolves, but also because the Pure are useful against the Idigam. Even with this reduced hostility, I would be extra wary of Predatory Kings for hopefully obvious reasons\u2026 and I may have to be extra cautious with Ivory Claws, since pretty much all Forsaken count as their sacred prey just by being Forsaken\u2026 and then again, who knows when the Fire-Touched will decide that they\u2019re done trying to convert me to the Pure and ready to just try to kill me? Can\u2019t be too careful I suppose. If only they didn\u2019t take their oral history so seriously.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In another respect, if I had to deal with a Pure individual who really got on my nerves, It would bring me a great feeling of satisfaction to learn what their auspice was/would have been before they were inducted into the Pure. I would call the Pure individual by that auspice instead of their name - and I would also make jabs at them regarding their auspice. \u201cNot much of a spiritual guy, huh Ithaeur? No wonder you decided to join the Pure!&quot;. I would enjoy reminding them that all werewolves change in the sight of the moon, and even if they were never touched by &quot;the Whore-Moon\u2019s taint or whatever other cute name you guys like to call the moon\u201d, they would have received an auspice without Pure intervention. Obviously this would be more effective on those Pure who had to have their auspice removed. It wouldn\u2019t really be a worthwhile tactic for practical purposes, but it would get under their skin, and I would enjoy getting under the skin of an annoying Pure werewolf.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Elder Wolf</b>: Let\u2019s assume that I manage to survive long enough to reach this point for the purpose of discussion. I mean this is all hypothetical anyway. I mean it is certainly possible that my less than absolute hostile attitude towards the Pure and my lackadaisical attitude towards the oral history of the werewolves will make it harder for me to make allies. Then again, which is the shadowed half?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">While I would certainly be happy to give young cubs advice on whatever they are doing, chances are I will still remain active in my territory. I mean for one, werewolves have primal urge that pushes them to hunt, but aside from that - if I see something that needs to be done, I would rather do it myself rather than send someone else to do it. While I like the idea of being a mentor, I also think I wouldn\u2019t make a good mentor if I\u2019m always busy with my own work, but such is the way of things. There is always something that needs to be done, and I don\u2019t trust anyone more than myself (and my pack at this point) to accomplish whatever task needs completing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Chances are I would be a member of the Lodge of Crows at this point\u2026 not that anyone would know. By this point as well, I will have a massive web of contacts, allies, and resources - including those murder and madness spirits that you planned to send to kill my family and friends. Even so, I wouldn't fuck with you so long as you don\u2019t fuck with me (quid pro quo and all that). So long as it can be helped, I could make better use out of living Pure than dead Pure. They are an excellent warning system against the <i>Idigam</i>. If a bunch of Pure die and none of the Forsaken know why, it\u2019s probably because some <i>Idigam</i> is on the loose. While a Forsaken werewolf doesn\u2019t make it this far by trusting the Pure, they still have their place in the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If things go well for me, I would like it if I could find another Firstborn and bind it to a new tribe that takes the <i>Idigam</i> as their sacred prey. As I said, if Creator Wolf is available for this purpose, I feel like she would be great for thematic reasons. By available I mean not bound to another tribe - possible to find - possible to aid and bind to a tribe at some point, even if it would prove to be my greatest challenge. If Creator Wolf is not available, I\u2019ll find another Firstborn, or I\u2019ll find a Secondborn or something of reasonably comparable power.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Of course forming a tribe is only the first step. After that, the hunt goes on. I don\u2019t know how many <i>Idigam</i> exist, so I\u2019ll just have to keep on hunting them until I die. It won\u2019t be easy, but hopefully by this point I could hope to challenge one - myself and my web of allies.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","user":"oeruli","date":".  Fixing grammatical errors. I doubt I got them all. 11-12-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T14:03:58-08:00","id":1157989,"title":"","content":"Now that is a very well thought out answer, and I like it a lot. I actually use Creator Wolf In a lot of different games in my canon, and though though she is a Pure totem in my game universe, there is always the chance that the thing that Fenris Ur is looking for in Iraq is also Creator Wolf xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 11-12-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T15:30:57-08:00","id":1158008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1157989#post1157989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that is a very well thought out answer, and I like it a lot. I actually use Creator Wolf In a lot of different games in my canon, and though though she is a Pure totem in my game universe, there is always the chance that the thing that Fenris Ur is looking for in Iraq is also Creator Wolf xD</div> </div> </div> </div>If Danu-Ur is in Iraq with Fenris-Ur and a goodly chunk of his Blood Talons, then this is probably going to be a big pain. Then again, my goal is to find a Wolf God and petition its aid against a host of other gods of chaos. In this variant, I would be racing against one of the biggest, baddest Wolf Gods of all in a quest to find another Wolf God so I can petition her to help me against said host of gods. I suppose no one said it would be easy. It could make for a fun chronicle, though!<br /> <br /> Realistically speaking, the most probable result is that my pack and I becomes a collection of very ugly corpses - averaging 5 pieces per corpse. This is what happens when you toy with gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:20:41-08:00","id":1158013,"title":"","content":"That is why you usually try to bring a bunch of expendable meat shiel- I mean friends along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T16:54:34-08:00","id":1158021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1158013#post1158013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is why you usually try to bring a bunch of expendable meat shiel- I mean friends along.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis Ivory Claw (wo)man would like to point out that expendable meat shields is our tactic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:22:38-08:00","id":1158028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1158021#post1158021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThis Ivory Claw (wo)man would like to point out that expendable meat shields is our tactic</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this Fire-Touched will say that we have the largest numbers, we know a thing about meat shields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:01:29-08:00","id":1158050,"title":"","content":"This meat shield thinks you're both out of line","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T19:34:00-08:00","id":1158057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1158050#post1158050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This meat shield thinks you're both out of line</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t matter what the meat shield thinks, you\u2019re supposed to be standing between me and the cowardly silver daggers of those Moon loving pansies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T21:21:21-08:00","id":1158071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1158013#post1158013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is why you usually try to bring a bunch of expendable meat shiel- I mean friends along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! Yes, of course! I mean <b>friends</b>! Trusted and valued friends who will keep their territories in some sort of order and all that - the easier to tell the difference between business as usual and <i>Idigam</i> invasion.<br /> <br /> Jeez, no wonder other werewolf packs don't get along...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T23:07:03-08:00","id":1158092,"title":"","content":"All this talk about meat shields... sounds like a waste of good meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T06:52:28-08:00","id":1158159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1129318-you-as-a-werewolf?p=1158092#post1158092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this talk about meat shields... sounds like a waste of good meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is plenty left, don\u2019t worry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:58:15-08:00","id":1159554,"title":"","content":"If I were Pure, I'd be a Predator King. Simple life, hunting for food, protecting the wild, fighting for sex etc...<br /> <br /> But more likely I'd be one of the Forsaken. Considering my gentle nature and violent daydreams I'd probably manifest those daydreams after the First Change, so Blood Talons probably. Ithaeur, simply because I am insanely interested in spirits, lore and animism. I'd be from a Forsaken family, where wolf-blooded kids are taught the Secret History, the First Tongue, and the traditions of the tribe(s).<br /> <br /> As a cub, I'd be super cautious and utilize Hisil to the best of my skill. Form pacts, learn gifts, study the landscape etc...Anything to help my pack gain the upper hand, should they need to do battle on Amahan Iduth's side of the Veil.<br /> <br /> As an elder, I'd be the alpha of a pack of wolf-spirits (and the shaman of my own pack); terrorizing enemy spirit-territory, killing pure-friendly spirits when befriending is futile, poisoning or destroying loci...anything to cut my Sacred Prey from their spiritual sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Dam da namsithim.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12696-lost-his-mind","name":"Lost-His-Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T08:43:47-08:00","id":1162728,"title":"","content":"I've been mildly obsessed with categorizing myself in the WoD splats for some time now, so this is a great thread for me! <br /> <br /> I wouldn't be Pure or Bale Hound, that's for sure. Forsaken or Ghost Wolf for me. But let me write out my thoughts. <br /> <br /> So, first I went for my <b>Auspice</b>. While my natural inclination is to go for Ithaeur, I actually went and found out what the moon's phase was when I was born. And according to reality, I would be <b>Elodoth</b>. <br /> <br /> While not my first choice, it actually fits me very well. I often find myself being the mediator or even just de-escalating confrontations and seeking common ground. I try not to take information or knowledge for granted, and instead figure things out for myself. The judge/diplomat/investigator Hat for the Elodoth would actually fit me quite well. <br /> <br /> With Auspice decided, next comes Tribe. The Blood Talon, the Storm Lords and the Hunters in Darkness are out, since they are all pretty extreme in one way or another and I can't see myself joining any of them. The tough choice is between the Iron Masters and the Bone Shadows. The Bone Shadows appeal to my curiosity and my natural inclination to learn more. The Iron Masters conversely appeal to my creativity and the urge to innovate and figure out unorthodox ways of doing things. <br /> <br /> And of course if I wanted to step outside the dogma of the Forsaken, there's always being a Ghost Wolf. <br /> <br /> While I'd like to think I'd cut it as a Ghost Wolf (and my asocial inclinations might push me that way), the perks and advantages of having the social structure of a tribe would probably be too useful to give up on. As long as I keep my skepticism about the dogma of the tribe to myself, I'd be okay, right? <br /> <br /> Right...<br /> <br /> While I'd want to be connected to the insights that the Iron Masters would pursue, I'd probably lean more towards the ethos of the <b>Bone Shadows</b>. I can easily see a sort of melding of their philosophies in my werewolf alter-ego, with him pursuing harmony between the spirits of urban and technological growth with the spirits of nature and existing communities. A little Children-of-Gaia meets Glass-Walkers vibe. An urban shaman-scholar with a penchant for resolving disputes. <br /> <br /> So. <b>Bone Shadow. Elodoth. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> This was fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}